## Investigation Finding

The existing `gridOriginAuthorityGate` already has a source-backed row-domain candidate (`sourceDomainRowAnchorCandidate:true` in fixture assertions) derived from selected line headers plus `/LineMark` record/group alignment. It does not promote that candidate into page-space origin authority:

- `/LineMark` interval evidence is source-backed and reference-free.
- `/PageMark` Y-value evidence is explicitly `referenceBacked:true` because it is tied to `currentProjectionOriginY`.
- `pageSpaceOriginCandidate` remains `null`.
- `pageSpaceOriginCandidateReady` remains `false`.
- `promotionReady` remains `false`.
- Render blockers include `document-text-grid-origin-reference-backed` and `page-space-y-origin-unproven`.

Conclusion: the only page-space origin candidate is still reference/residual-backed, so render admission remains blocked as required.

